Recompiler: vector unit register 0 is never written.

What it fixes: VF0 is the constant (0, 0, 0, 1) and the unit drops any write to it (VUops.cpp: the destination register of an
operation with fd = 0 is a dummy; qmtc2 and lqc2 skip VF0). The recompiler wrote it: qmtc2 to VF0, lqc2 to VF0, and every
operation whose destination field is 0 (vmove, vmr32, vabs, vftoi, vitof, the Special1 arithmetic and min/max). Now the
translator emits a comment instead, decided from the destination field of the word (sa for the Special1 table below 0x30, rt for
the Special2 ones above); lqc2 to VF0 still makes the load and drops the value.

How it was verified: tests/conformance family "vu0", forms fd=vf0 / ft=vf0 / vf=0: vabs, vmove, vmr32, lqc2, qmtc2 and every
arithmetic form with fd = 0 differed before (VF0 got the result), none after.
Reach in the game: one site writes VF0 (an lqc2 at 0x102cbc, 1 of 1,059); no arithmetic site has fd = 0. It restores a saved
VF0, which is (0, 0, 0, 1) when it was saved by this runtime, so the effect is nil unless a save holds another value.

Original work for this repository (no code from another project).

--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/vu_translator.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/vu_translator.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,27 @@
         uint8_t rd = inst.rd;
         uint8_t sa = inst.sa;
 
+        // VF0 is (0, 0, 0, 1) and a write to it is dropped (VUops.cpp: the destination is a dummy register). The destination
+        // field of the operations that write a vector register: sa for the Special1 table below 0x30, rt for these Special2 ones.
+        if (format >= COP2_CO)
+        {
+            const uint8_t func = static_cast<uint8_t>(inst.function & 0x3F);
+            uint8_t destination = 0xFF;
+            if (func >= 0x3C)
+            {
+                const uint8_t vu_func = static_cast<uint8_t>((((inst.raw >> 6) & 0x1F) << 2) | (inst.raw & 0x3));
+                if ((vu_func >= VU0_S2_VITOF0 && vu_func <= VU0_S2_VFTOI15) || vu_func == VU0_S2_VABS ||
+                    vu_func == VU0_S2_VMOVE || vu_func == VU0_S2_VMR32)
+                    destination = inst.rt;
+            }
+            else if (func < 0x30)
+            {
+                destination = inst.sa;
+            }
+            if (destination == 0)
+                return "// the destination is VF0 (read-only): no write";
+        }
+
         switch (format)
         {
         case COP2_QMFC2:
@@ -64,6 +85,8 @@
             }
         }
         case COP2_QMTC2:
+            if (rd == 0)
+                return "// QMTC2 to VF0 ignored (VF0 is read-only)";
             return fmt::format("ctx->vu0_vf[{}] = _mm_castsi128_ps(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}));", rd, rt);
         case COP2_CTC2:
